WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.600
"For example, if I want to..."
— "Compare where I started at Point A with where I am now."

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.200
Exactly. Let's make it concrete: say "I want to become a Department Director." What's your name?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:18.600
— "Nahed."
"Nahed! Got it."

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.400
Say I want to be a Department Director — wait, are you already one?
— "I am!"

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.000
What's the role above you? — "General Manager."
Then the goal is: "I want to become General Manager!"

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:40.200
So Point A — where you stand right now — is Department Director, with the skills and network you've built here.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.200
Reaching General Manager — that's the next stage (Point B).

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:54.300
So the real question you ask yourself is: "What concrete steps will take me from here to General Manager?"

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.000
And that is what we call a milestone goal.
